Files: Cargo.lock
Copyright: 2026 Boswas Group
License: LicenseRef-Boswas-Internal
Comment: This file pins the Rust crates the build downloads from crates.io.
 The programs are linked statically with the following crates and with the
 Rust standard library; each is copyright its authors (The Rust Project
 Developers; Dan Gohman and the Bytecode Alliance for rustix and
 linux-raw-sys; the Smithay project for drm, drm-ffi, drm-sys and drm-fourcc;
 the landlock contributors; Lokathor for bytemuck; David Tolnay for
 thiserror; the RustCrypto developers for zeroize; and the contributors of
 bitflags, enumflags2 and libc) and is used here under the MIT licence
 (called Expat below), which all of them offer, most of them as an
 alternative to Apache-2.0:
 bitflags, bytemuck, drm, drm-ffi, drm-fourcc, drm-sys, enumflags2,
 landlock, libc, linux-raw-sys, rustix, thiserror, zeroize.
 Crates used only while building (resvg and its dependencies, fontdue,
 serde_json) are not part of the programs.

Files: build.rs
Copyright: 2026 Boswas Group
License: LicenseRef-Boswas-Internal and Expat
Comment: build.rs itself is a Boswas file. It is listed here because it
 puts third-party material into the programs: the Rust crates described
 under Cargo.lock (Expat), and a rasterised atlas of the printable ASCII
 glyphs of Orbitron Medium, the Boswas OS brand typeface (see the next
 paragraph).

Files: desktop/fonts/orbitron/*
Copyright: 2018 The Orbitron Project Authors (https://github.com/theleagueof/orbitron)
License: OFL-1.1
Comment: Orbitron, the Boswas OS brand typeface, in the Boswas OS source
 repository (not in this package's directory). The programs embed bitmaps
 of its printable ASCII glyphs, made at build time from
 Orbitron-Medium.ttf; the font file itself is not shipped by this package.
 Reserved Font Name: "Orbitron".

